        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Israel, in old times when they entered the land of Egypt under the kingdom of Moab and Media... Jacob&#x27;s prayer&#x27; — explicit GENESIS CROSS-REFERENCE locking the brothers into covenant-history. References Genesis 46 (Jacob&#x27;s family entering Egypt) reframed anachronistically through &#x27;kingdom of Moab and Media&#x27; (a characteristically Meqabyan composite-historical-geography — the same telescoping appears at 2:2 &#x27;land of the Chaldeans, in Midian, and in the country of the Medes&#x27; for the brothers&#x27; homeland). The patriarchal-prayer reference connects the brothers&#x27; trust-in-God to Jacob&#x27;s prayer at Bethel (Gen 28:20-22) + the Moses-praying-at-Marah pattern + the Hannah-praying-in-Shiloh pattern. Tewahedo prayer-tradition reads 2:26 as the brothers&#x27; alignment with the entire OT prayer-trajectory.</p></aside>',
