        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>Completion of the first death-and-resurrection scene (paired with seed 2:27). The brothers die at the king&#x27;s command and are restored — the resurrection-cycle that DEFINES the Meqabyan martyrology and prefigures 3 Mq&#x27;s developed resurrection-doctrine. Parallels the seven-fold-martyrdom cycle of LXX 2 Maccabees 7 (but with the distinctive Meqabyan number-shift to five-brothers + the rise-again capacity actualized within the narrative rather than promised-for-the-eschaton). Per Horovitz 1905 + CROSS_REFERENCE_APPENDIX §10 the seed-buried argument at 8:22-32 is the STRONGEST PAULINE PARALLEL to 1 Cor 15:36-38 in the entire trilogy — the 2:27-28 in-narrative resurrection is the EARLY ANTHROPOLOGICAL anchor that the 8:22 + 10:5 (patriarch-burial) + 36:45 (closing capstone) arguments will systematize.</p></aside>',
