        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 9: APOSTATES AND HERETICS CATALOG — idol-worshipers + ROOT-CHEWERS (sorcerers using herbal-magic) + the peoples of specific geographic regions whose religious practices fall outside the covenant. The &#x27;root-chewers&#x27; (ስርቆም ቆራጮች) is a distinctive Meqabyan-Geʽez category for SORCERERS-WHO-USE-HERBAL-PHARMACOLOGY-FOR-DIVINATION — paralleling Deut 18:10-11 forbidden-divination list (necromancer + diviner + sorcerer + wizard + medium); Galatians 5:20 pharmakeia (&#x27;witchcraft&#x27; / drug-sorcery); Revelation 9:21 + 18:23 + 22:15 pharmakoi (&#x27;sorcerers&#x27;). The MERCY-RAIN geography (Galaboh + Lebanon + Gilead + Elam at 9:1-2) precedes the catalog as God&#x27;s-mercy-region contrast — the catalog at v. 3 names those EXCLUDED from the mercy-rain by their religious violations. The chapter functions as a Meqabyan-distinctive negative-catechesis (who-is-NOT-in-the-covenant-community).</p></aside>',
