        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 20 — HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR (per source-fidelity note): post-resurrection-cycle homiletic + martyr-cult formation. The chapter&#x27;s likely thematic-content: in the narrative-progression after the first martyrdom-cycle (Chs 3-4) and the homiletic-instruction (Chs 5-7 + 8-19), Ch 20 likely transitions to MARTYR-CULT formation themes — the institutional-memorialization of the Maqabean-martyrs. Parallels: 4 MACCABEES 17:8-22 (Maccabean-martyrs&#x27; monumentalization + the inscription-of-virtue); 2 MACCABEES 7:38 + 8:1-7 (Judas Maccabeus&#x27;s vow + revolt-following the martyrdoms); HEBREWS 11:35 (the &#x27;others were tortured, not accepting deliverance; that they might obtain a better resurrection&#x27; — read as Maccabean-martyr reference in patristic tradition); MARTYRDOM OF POLYCARP 18 (the martyr-cult&#x27;s anniversary celebrations); CYPRIAN Epistle 22 (memorial-mass for the martyrs). Tewahedo Sǝnkǝsar (Synaxarium) preserves the Maccabean-martyrs&#x27; feast-day commemoration (1 August in EOTC calendar) drawing on this chapter&#x27;s likely martyr-cult institution-narrative.</p></aside>',
