        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR — likely development of MARTYR-INTERCESSION theme. The martyr-intercession-doctrine: martyrs in heaven intercede for the church on earth. Parallels: REVELATION 6:9-11 (the souls-under-the-altar cry-for-vindication — paired with 2 Mq 10:1 γ.4.8.C entry); REVELATION 8:3-4 (the prayers-of-all-saints rising-with-incense); 2 MACCABEES 15:12-16 (the dream-vision of Onias + Jeremiah praying for Jerusalem); ORIGEN Exhortation to Martyrdom 30 (martyrs-pray-for-fellow-believers); MARTYRDOM OF POLYCARP 19 (Polycarp&#x27;s intercession after death); CYPRIAN Letter 60 (martyrs-as-priest-advocates). Tewahedo intercessory-doctrine explicitly preserves the martyr-as-intercessor framework integrated with Marian + saintly + angelic intercession. The Meqabyan doctrinal contribution: the FIVE MAQABEAN MARTYRS function as the TEWAHEDO-CANONICAL martyr-intercession exemplars alongside the Forty Martyrs of Sebaste + St George + the Apostolic-Era martyrs.</p></aside>',
