        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 21 — HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR: faithfulness-under-threat theme. The chapter likely develops the Maqabean-martyrs&#x27; faithfulness as MODEL for everyday-believer faithfulness — paralleling the 2 Mq Ch 6 mother&#x27;s-exhortation + 3 Mq Ch 6 suffering-and-perseverance themes (γ.4.8.C + γ.4.8.D entries). Direct biblical parallels: 1 PETER 4:12-19 (Petrine suffering-theology); HEBREWS 10:32-39 (need-of-patience + faith-toward-saving-of-the-soul); REVELATION 2:10 (&#x27;be thou faithful unto death, and I will give thee a crown of life&#x27;); 2 TIMOTHY 2:11-13 (&#x27;if we suffer, we shall also reign with him; if we deny him, he also will deny us&#x27;); 1 MACCABEES 2:50-64 (Mattathias&#x27;s deathbed-exhortation to faithfulness). Patristic-tradition: TERTULLIAN De Fuga in Persecutione (the flee-or-stand-firm controversy); ORIGEN Exhortation to Martyrdom; AUGUSTINE Letter 185 (the political-theology of faithful-resistance). Tewahedo confessional-tradition preserves faithfulness-unto-death as one of the four-cardinal-Christian-virtues (faith + hope + charity + faithfulness — Tewahedo expansion of the Pauline-three).</p></aside>',
