        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR — likely development of COVENANT-FIDELITY theme synthesizing the chapter&#x27;s faithfulness-and-wisdom catalog. The covenant-fidelity theme parallels: DEUTERONOMY 7:9 (&#x27;the LORD thy God, he is God, the faithful God, which keepeth covenant and mercy with them that love him and keep his commandments to a thousand generations&#x27; — paired with mq2 3:9 γ.4.8.C entry); PSALM 89:1-37 (the Davidic covenant-fidelity psalm); HEBREWS 6:13-20 (God&#x27;s-immutable-counsel for the seed-of-Abraham); LUKE 1:54-55 + 1:72-75 (Mary&#x27;s-Magnificat + Zechariah&#x27;s-Benedictus covenant-fidelity recapitulation); 2 CORINTHIANS 1:20 (in Christ all God&#x27;s promises are Yes and Amen). Tewahedo soteriology preserves covenant-fidelity as the integrating-anchor for the Tewahedo-Hayyamanot (Tewahedo-confessional-faith) — the canonical-EOTC Christological-covenantal framework. The Meqabyan chapter likely synthesizes the chapter&#x27;s homiletic into covenant-fidelity-as-telos.</p></aside>',
