        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 22 — HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR: covenant-renewal-homiletic + rebuke-of-king theme. The chapter likely develops the prophetic-rebuke-of-the-king theme established earlier in the trilogy (cf. 2 Mq 2:1 prophet Re&#x27;ay confronts Maqabis-of-Moab γ.4.8 seed; 1 Mq 7:1 sons&#x27; direct-address-to-king γ.4.8.B entry). Direct biblical parallels for the rebuke-of-king pattern: NATHAN-TO-DAVID 2 SAMUEL 12 (Nathan&#x27;s &#x27;thou art the man&#x27; parable-rebuke); ELIJAH-TO-AHAB 1 KINGS 21:17-29 (after Naboth&#x27;s-vineyard); ELIJAH-TO-AHAZIAH 2 KINGS 1:1-17; AMOS-TO-AMAZIAH-AT-BETHEL Amos 7:10-17; ISAIAH-TO-AHAZ Isaiah 7:1-17; JEREMIAH-TO-JEHOIAKIM Jeremiah 36:29-30; JOHN-THE-BAPTIST-TO-HEROD-ANTIPAS Mark 6:17-29 par. The Meqabyan chapter likely extends the prophetic-rebuke-of-king pattern to a STRUCTURAL-CULMINATION before the chapter&#x27;s covenant-renewal theme (mirroring 2 Mq Ch 3&#x27;s pit-immersion-conversion + Ch 4 idols-and-sorcerers-purge γ.4.8.C entries).</p></aside>',
