        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR — likely development of FEAR-OF-THE-LORD as wisdom-foundation theme (paralleling 3 Mq 6:7 γ.4.8.D entry). The fear-of-the-LORD theme is the classic Wisdom-literature anchor: PROVERBS 1:7 + 9:10 (&#x27;the fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom&#x27;); PSALM 111:10 (the same formula); SIRACH 1:11-30 (the fear-of-the-LORD catalog); ECCLESIASTES 12:13 (&#x27;fear God, and keep his commandments: for this is the whole duty of man&#x27;); WISDOM OF SOLOMON 1:1-15 (the foundational royal-fear-of-God treatise); ACTS 9:31 (the church walking in fear-of-the-Lord and comfort-of-the-Holy-Ghost). Patristic-tradition: BARSANUPHIUS Letter 168 (monastic-fear-of-God as foundation — paired with 3 Mq 6:7 entry); JOHN CLIMACUS Ladder Step 1 (the renunciation-of-the-world rooted in fear-of-God). Tewahedo monastic-pedagogy explicitly grounds the spiritual-formation-rubric in fear-of-the-Lord as Step-Zero before complete-repentance (3 Mq 4:34 γ.4.8 seed).</p></aside>',
