        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 24 — HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR: divine-justice theme. The chapter likely develops divine-justice as the integrating-anchor for the chapter&#x27;s prophetic-confrontation arc. The divine-justice theme parallels: PSALM 9:7-8 + 11:7 + 96:13 + 98:9 (God-judges-the-world-with-righteousness); DEUTERONOMY 32:4 (&#x27;he is the Rock, his work is perfect: for all his ways are judgment: a God of truth and without iniquity, just and right is he&#x27;); ROMANS 2:1-11 (Pauline-divine-impartiality at judgment); 2 THESSALONIANS 1:5-10 (the righteous-judgment of God at parousia); REVELATION 16:5-7 (thou-art-righteous-O-Lord acclamations at judgment-pouring); WISDOM 12:12-22 (the philosophical-treatment of divine-justice). Patristic-tradition: AUGUSTINE City of God 19-22 (the most-extended treatment of divine-justice + the two-cities eschatology); GREGORY THE GREAT Moralia in Iob (the foundational Latin Job-commentary on divine-justice-and-Job&#x27;s-suffering). Tewahedo theological tradition preserves divine-justice as the integrating-anchor for the trilogy&#x27;s anti-Sebelyanos/Ṣiruṣaydan polemic-architecture.</p></aside>',
