        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>**ETHIOPIA NAMED** (alongside Saba/Sheba + India + Nubia) — the first of two explicit Ethiopia-references in 1 Meqabyan (paired with 28:38 at γ.4.8.B-detail-wave). The mention is GEOGRAPHICALLY-IMPORTANT: Ethiopia + Saba (Sheba) + India + Nubia form the eastern + southern horizon of the Hellenistic-Aksumite world. Saba/Sheba = the Solomonic-tradition source (1 Kings 10 + 2 Chron 9 + the Tewahedo Kǝbrä Nägäśt Solomonic-dynasty claim); India = the Apostolic-mission destination (per Eusebius Hist. Eccl. 5.10 Pantaenus to India; the Thomasine tradition); Nubia = the immediate-Northern-neighbor; Ethiopia = the home of Frumentius-the-Tewahedo-founder. The geographical-self-naming of Ethiopia within the canonical Meqabyan text is a DIAGNOSTIC ETHIOPIAN-SELF-RECOGNITION moment, locating the text within the Aksumite-Ethiopian Christian self-understanding. Per memory `project_v1_terminus`: Ethiopia-named is a Tewahedo-uniqueness-angle the buyer-demo surfaces visibly.</p></aside>',
