        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 29: &#x27;So also with kings and princes — those who disregard God&#x27;s word, who do not do his will, who do not give their wages to those who serve in good things...&#x27; — the COVENANT-EXCHANGE FORMULA in classic Hebrew-Bible mode: &#x27;Do good for good and evil for evil.&#x27; The reciprocity-principle is the integrating-anchor for the Exodus-chapter retelling (vv. 1-4 brick-making + Moses/Aaron sent + drowning of Pharaoh). The covenant-exchange structure parallels: DEUTERONOMY 28 (blessings-for-obedience + curses-for-disobedience covenant); LEVITICUS 26 (the parallel covenant-formula); the Deuteronomistic History&#x27;s repeated-pattern (&#x27;Israel did evil... the LORD raised an oppressor... they cried out... the LORD raised a deliverer&#x27;); ROMANS 2:6-11 (Pauline &#x27;who will render to every man according to his deeds&#x27;). Meqabyan applies the formula AGAINST Pharaoh + Ṣiruṣaydan: divine-justice is reciprocal-and-impartial, regardless of imperial-power.</p></aside>',
