        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>Covenant-honor-formula deepening (paired with seed 30:7 1 Sam 2:30 covenant-honor): the verse develops the &#x27;them that honor me I will honor, and they that despise me shall be lightly esteemed&#x27; formula. Patristic-extended-reception of 1 Sam 2:30: GREGORY OF NYSSA De Vita Moysis 2.260-262 (honor-and-dishonor parallels); JOHN CHRYSOSTOM Homilies on 1 Samuel; AUGUSTINE Enarrationes in Psalmos 30 + 70 (the honor-formula in Psalter); AMBROSE Letters 73 + 76 (the political application — Theodosius&#x27;s penance + the Callinicum incident). The covenant-honor-formula parallels: PSALM 91:14-16 (&#x27;because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name&#x27;); JOHN 12:26 (&#x27;if any man serve me, him will my Father honour&#x27;); ROMANS 2:6-11 (Pauline-divine-impartiality); SIRACH 3:6 (honor-father-and-mother formula echo). Tewahedo soteriology preserves the covenant-honor-formula as the canonical-anchor for Tewahedo-imperial-and-monastic confessional-tradition.</p></aside>',
