        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>LIGHT-FILLED HEAVENLY CITY for good-kings (paired with seed 33:1 manna-as-bread-of-angels). The chapter develops a CONTRAST between the light-filled-heavenly-city (vv. 8-10) awaiting righteous-kings and the GEHENNA prepared for the wicked. The light-filled-city imagery parallels: REVELATION 21:23 (&#x27;and the city had no need of the sun, neither of the moon, to shine in it: for the glory of God did lighten it, and the Lamb is the light thereof&#x27;); ISAIAH 60:19-20 (Zion&#x27;s-eschatological-light); 1 ENOCH 25:5-7 + 51:1-5 (the city-of-the-righteous in the Watchers + Parables sections); 4 EZRA 7:88-99 (the seven-fold-glory of the righteous-dead). Meqabyan&#x27;s distinctive contribution: the city is specifically reserved for RIGHTEOUS-KINGS (the chapter develops the royal-soteriology that pairs Ch 7&#x27;s king&#x27;s-duties + Ch 6&#x27;s heavenly-palace-ekphrasis into a coherent Meqabyan ROYAL-ESCHATOLOGY).</p></aside>',
