        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 35 — HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR: penultimate chapter, immediately before final-resurrection-capstone (Ch 36 seed: 36:22 Abraham-my-friend + 36:29 Hellenistic-deity dating-anchor + 36:45 resurrection-tricolon capstone + γ.4.8.B 36:1 Macedonia/Amalekites + 36:43 Gen 15:6 Abraham-believed-God). The penultimate-chapter likely serves as DOXOLOGICAL-PREPARATION for the final-capstone — paralleling the trilogy&#x27;s structural-rhythm of intermediate-doxology + transition-to-final-arc. The penultimate-chapter pattern parallels: PSALM 149-150 (the Psalter&#x27;s penultimate + final praise-psalms); REVELATION 21 (the penultimate-revelation preparation for Ch 22&#x27;s coming-Lord doxology); 1 ENOCH 107 (the penultimate-Enoch chapter preparing 108&#x27;s final-doxology — γ.4.4 structure); JUBILEES 49 (the penultimate-Jubilees chapter preparing 50&#x27;s final-Sabbath-doxology — γ.4.5 structure). The Meqabyan penultimate-chapter likely articulates the final-faithfulness-summons before the resurrection-capstone declares the consequence.</p></aside>',
