        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR — likely development of FINAL-EXHORTATION-TO-FAITHFULNESS theme. The final-exhortation theme parallels: DEUTERONOMY 30:11-20 (Moses&#x27;s-final-exhortation-to-choose-life); JOSHUA 24:14-15 (&#x27;choose you this day whom ye will serve&#x27;); 1 SAMUEL 12:20-25 (Samuel&#x27;s-farewell-address); 2 TIMOTHY 4:1-8 (Paul&#x27;s-final-charge); 2 PETER 1:12-15 + 3:14-18 (Peter&#x27;s-final-reminder); JUDE 17-25 (the final-doxological-exhortation); REVELATION 22:11-21 (the final-revelation-exhortation). Patristic-tradition: IGNATIUS OF ANTIOCH Letters (the seven-letters&#x27;-final-exhortations); CLEMENT 65 (the closing-doxological-exhortation); POLYCARP To the Philippians 14 (the final-exhortation pattern). Tewahedo confessional-tradition preserves the final-exhortation-to-faithfulness as the structural-anchor of catechetical-baptismal preparation. The Meqabyan chapter likely articulates the final-exhortation gathering the trilogy&#x27;s themes into faithfulness-unto-resurrection.</p></aside>',
