        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>Final-capstone-doxology deepening (paired with seed 36:22 Abraham-my-friend-Isaac-my-favored-Jacob-my-beloved triple-formula + 36:29 Hellenistic-deity Apollon-Artemis-Serapion dating-anchor + 36:45 DOCTRINAL-CAPSTONE resurrection-tricolon double-Amen + γ.4.8.B 36:1 Macedonia+Amalekites Sheol/heaven + 36:43 Gen 15:6 Abraham-believed-God Rom 4:3 + Jas 2:23). The verse develops the closing-doxology architecture — the final-warning preceding the resurrection-tricolon. The final-warning-before-doxology pattern parallels: DEUTERONOMY 32:46-47 (&#x27;set your hearts unto all the words which I testify among you this day, which ye shall command your children to observe to do, all the words of this law: For it is not a vain thing for you&#x27;); JOSHUA 24:25-28 (the great-stone-at-Shechem witness-against-Israel); 2 PETER 3:17-18 (the keep-yourselves-from-being-led-away + grow-in-grace closing); JUDE 20-23 (the build-up-yourselves-and-keep-yourselves-in-the-love-of-God closing); REVELATION 22:18-19 (the anathema-against-adding-or-taking-away). Tewahedo canonical tradition preserves the final-warning-before-doxology as integral to the book-closing architectural-pattern.</p></aside>',
