        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And Abraham BELIEVED IN GOD; AND THEREFORE IT WAS RECKONED TO HIM AS RIGHTEOUSNESS; and his hope on earth was fulfilled — his wife Sarah, even after she had grown old, bore the son Isaac&#x27; — DIRECT CITATION OF GENESIS 15:6 (&#x27;And he believed in the LORD; and he counted it to him for righteousness&#x27;), THE SAME VERSE cited by Paul at ROMANS 4:3 (&#x27;Abraham believed God, and it was counted unto him for righteousness&#x27;) AND by James at JAMES 2:23 (&#x27;And the scripture was fulfilled which saith, Abraham believed God, and it was imputed unto him for righteousness: and he was called the Friend of God&#x27;). The pairing of this verse with seed 36:22 (&#x27;Abraham my friend&#x27; triple-formula) REPLICATES THE EXACT NEW TESTAMENT ABRAHAM-TYPOLOGY: faith-reckoned-as-righteousness (Gen 15:6 / Rom 4 / Jas 2) + friendship-with-God (Isa 41:8 + 2 Chr 20:7 + Jas 2:23). The Meqabyan-Pauline-Jacobean Abraham-typology is one of the trilogy&#x27;s strongest direct-NT parallels.</p></aside>',
